**EXCERPT FROM THE MASTER SERVICE AGREEMENT**  
**BETWEEN**  
**TECHNOVA SOLUTIONS, INC.**  
**AND**  
**GREENFIELD SMART SYSTEMS, LLC**  
**DATED: October 1, 2023**  

**1. DEFINITIONS**  
For the purposes of this Agreement, the following terms shall have the meanings ascribed to them below:

1.1 “Connected Devices” refers to any and all electronic devices that communicate and interact over the Internet, including but not limited to smart thermostats, security cameras, and wearables, as detailed in Exhibit A.

1.2 “Sensors” denotes the hardware components utilized to collect data from the physical environment, including but not limited to temperature sensors, humidity sensors, and motion detectors, as detailed in Exhibit B.

1.3 “Data Collection” refers to the systematic gathering of data from Connected Devices and Sensors, as outlined in Section 3 of this Agreement.

1.4 “Smart Systems” indicates integrated systems that utilize data from Connected Devices and Sensors to perform automated actions and enhance user experience, as defined in Section 4 of this Agreement.

**2. PARTIES**  
2.1 TechNova Solutions, Inc. (“TechNova”), located at 123 Innovation Drive, San Francisco, CA 94107, is a leading provider of IoT (Internet of Things) solutions and data analytics services. TechNova shall be responsible for the development, deployment, and maintenance of the Smart Systems.

2.2 Greenfield Smart Systems, LLC (“Greenfield”), located at 456 Sustainability Avenue, Austin, TX 78701, specializes in environmental monitoring and management solutions. Greenfield shall provide access to its network of sensors and assist in data collection efforts as specified herein.

**3. DATA COLLECTION**  
3.1 Greenfield shall deploy 500 units of the EcoSensor Model 2023, equipped with humidity and temperature sensors, across various locations in Central Park, New York City, starting November 1, 2023.

3.2 TechNova shall develop a cloud-based data aggregation platform to collect and analyze data from the EcoSensor Model 2023 devices. The platform will utilize AWS (Amazon Web Services) infrastructure to ensure scalability and security.

3.3 Data collected shall include, but not be limited to, temperature readings, humidity levels, and user interaction data. Greenfield will ensure that all data collection complies with local and federal regulations, including the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) and the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR).

**4. SMART SYSTEMS DEVELOPMENT**  
4.1 TechNova shall create Smart Systems that utilize real-time data from the EcoSensor Model 2023 to optimize environmental conditions in Central Park. The systems will include automated irrigation controls, environmental alerts, and user engagement features.

4.2 The Smart Systems will be tested in a pilot program scheduled to begin on January 15, 2024, and will run for a duration of six months. The pilot program will involve collaboration with the New York City Department of Parks and Recreation.

4.3 Feedback from the pilot program shall be reviewed by both parties on a bi-weekly basis, and necessary adjustments shall be made to the Smart Systems in accordance with the feedback received.

**5. RESPONSIBILITIES OF THE PARTIES**  
5.1 TechNova shall be responsible for:

5.1.1 Developing the software applications for data processing and visualization.

5.1.2 Maintaining the cloud infrastructure to ensure uninterrupted data access.

5.1.3 Providing technical support and training for Greenfield’s personnel on the use of Smart Systems.

5.2 Greenfield shall be responsible for:

5.2.1 Installing and maintaining the EcoSensor Model 2023 units at designated locations.

5.2.2 Collecting and transmitting data to TechNova’s cloud platform in real time.

5.2.3 Coordinating with local stakeholders, including the New York City Department of Environmental Protection, to ensure compliance with environmental standards.

**6. DATA OWNERSHIP AND USAGE**  
6.1 All data collected through the EcoSensor Model 2023 devices shall be jointly owned by TechNova and Greenfield. Both parties shall have equal rights to access and utilize the data for their respective purposes, provided that any commercial use requires prior written consent from both parties.

6.2 TechNova shall have the right to anonymize and aggregate the data for research purposes, including but not limited to academic publications and industry reports, provided that such usage does not disclose any personally identifiable information (PII).

**7. TERM AND TERMINATION**  
7.1 This Agreement shall commence on the Effective Date and shall continue for a period of three (3) years unless terminated earlier in accordance with this Section.

7.2 Either party may terminate this Agreement upon thirty (30) days written notice if the other party fails to cure any material breach of this Agreement within such notice period.

7.3 Upon termination, both parties shall return or destroy all proprietary information related to the Smart Systems and data collected, as per the confidentiality clauses outlined in Section 9.

**8. COMPENSATION**  
8.1 Greenfield shall compensate TechNova $250,000 for the development and deployment of the Smart Systems, payable in three installments: $100,000 upon contract signing, $75,000 upon completion of the pilot program, and $75,000 upon full deployment.

8.2 In addition to development fees, Greenfield shall pay TechNova an annual maintenance fee of $50,000 for continued support and infrastructure maintenance, due on the anniversary of the Agreement’s Effective Date.

**9. CONFIDENTIALITY**  
9.1 Each party agrees to keep confidential all proprietary information received from the other party during the term of this Agreement. This obligation shall survive termination for a period of five (5) years.

9.2 Confidential information shall not include information that is publicly known, independently developed, or disclosed pursuant to a legal obligation.

**10. INDEMNIFICATION**  
10.1 Each party agrees to indemnify and hold harmless the other party, its affiliates, and their respective officers, directors, employees, and agents from any claims, damages, losses, or expenses arising out of the negligent or willful misconduct of the indemnifying party in connection with this Agreement.

**11. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY**  
11.1 In no event shall either party be liable for any indirect, incidental, or consequential damages, including but not limited to loss of profits, arising out of or in connection with this Agreement.

**12. GOVERNING LAW**  
12.1 This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of California, without regard to its conflict of law principles.

